@@ -3,3 +3,21 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": 1 }, "/a~1b"); // 1
+resolvePointer({ a: 1 }, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the referenced value itself (not a copy) and never mutates its
+inputs. It throws a `JsonPointerError` if the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer or does not resolve to a
+value of the document (missing member, out-of-range or malformed array index, `-`, or a token applied to a
+non-object/array). Only own members of objects are considered. The URI fragment form (`#/a/b`) is not
+supported.
+
+Tests: `npm test`.
