+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) is that standard, and later features (e.g. JSON Patch, RFC 6902) will build on it, so it must be implemented once, correctly, and shared.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`: returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to within a JSON document.
+- It throws an error (`JsonPointerError`, also exported, a subclass of `Error`) when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 §3, §5), or when it does not resolve to a value of the document (RFC 6901 §4).
+- Not breaking: this is a new library surface; nothing existing changes (`src/` is currently empty).
+
+**Governing standard**: RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer), §3 syntax, §4 evaluation, §5 error handling. Documents are JSON per RFC 8259.
+
+**Out of scope**: the URI fragment representation (RFC 6901 §6, `#/a/b`), setting/removing/mutating values, JSON Patch, and building pointers from path segments.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: evaluating an RFC 6901 JSON Pointer against a JSON document, including syntax validation and failure to resolve.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code in `src/` (`src/index.ts` plus a pointer module) and tests runnable with `npm test`.
+- No new runtime dependencies; `package.json` changes only as needed to run TypeScript tests (see design).
